{
  "explanation": "The rules correct the HAPPO policy by increasing orders when downstream backlog is high and the pipeline is insufficient, while reducing orders when pipeline is excessive or demand has subsided. Rule 1 targets the downstream node (agent 0) with backlog, boosting orders if pipeline is low relative to recent demand. Rule 2 prevents over-ordering at any node when pipeline is already high compared to recent demand. Rule 3 reduces orders at upstream nodes when demand growth is low, avoiding persistent over-ordering after demand subsides. Rule 4 provides a mild boost for the downstream node when backlog exists but pipeline is moderate.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0 and pipeline < recent * 4",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, backlog / 2))"
    },
    {
      "when": "pipeline > recent * 5",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (pipeline - recent * 5) / 4))"
    },
    {
      "when": "agent >= 1 and growth < 1.1",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (1.1 - growth) * 10))"
    },
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0 and pipeline >= recent * 4",
      "delta": "min(3, max(0, backlog / 4))"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "The rules correct the HAPPO orders by increasing orders when backlog is high and pipeline is insufficient, while reducing orders when pipeline is excessive or demand growth is low. Rule 1 targets downstream nodes with high backlog and low pipeline, boosting orders. Rule 2 prevents over-ordering when pipeline is already large. Rule 3 reduces orders when demand growth is low, avoiding persistent over-ordering after demand subsides. Rule 4 provides a mild boost for moderate backlog.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "backlog > 10 and pipeline < 50",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, (backlog - 10) / 2))"
    },
    {
      "when": "pipeline > 60",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (pipeline - 60) / 5))"
    },
    {
      "when": "growth < 1.1",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (1.1 - growth) * 10))"
    },
    {
      "when": "backlog > 5 and pipeline < 40",
      "delta": "min(3, max(0, backlog / 4))"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "The rules correct HAPPO orders by increasing orders when downstream backlog is high and pipeline is low, while reducing orders when pipeline is excessive relative to backlog. Rule 1 targets severe downstream backlog with insufficient pipeline, adding up to 6 units. Rule 2 addresses moderate backlog with low pipeline, adding up to 3 units. Rule 3 prevents over-ordering when pipeline is already sufficient for current backlog, reducing orders by up to 4 units. Rule 4 slightly reduces orders when demand growth is low and pipeline is high, avoiding persistent over-ordering after demand subsides.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 10 and pipeline < 5",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, (backlog - 10) / 2))"
    },
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 5 and pipeline < 10",
      "delta": "min(3, max(0, (backlog - 5) / 3))"
    },
    {
      "when": "pipeline > backlog * 2 and backlog > 0",
      "delta": "-min(4, max(0, (pipeline - backlog * 2) / 5))"
    },
    {
      "when": "growth < 1.1 and pipeline > 20",
      "delta": "-min(2, max(0, (pipeline - 20) / 10))"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "The rules correct HAPPO orders by increasing orders when downstream backlog is high and pipeline is insufficient, while reducing orders when pipeline is excessive or demand has subsided. Rule 1 targets agent 0 with backlog and low pipeline coverage, boosting orders. Rule 2 reduces orders for any node when pipeline is very high relative to recent demand. Rule 3 reduces orders when demand growth is low, preventing over-ordering after demand subsides. Rule 4 provides a mild boost for agent 0 when backlog is moderate and pipeline is low.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 5 and pipeline < 4 * recent",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, backlog / 2))"
    },
    {
      "when": "pipeline > 5 * recent",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (pipeline - 5 * recent) / 4))"
    },
    {
      "when": "growth < 1.1 and pipeline > 2 * recent",
      "delta": "-min(6, max(0, (pipeline - 2 * recent) / 3))"
    },
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 2 and pipeline < 3 * recent",
      "delta": "min(3, max(0, backlog / 3))"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "The rules correct HAPPO orders to reduce downstream backlog while preventing over-ordering when pipeline is sufficient. Rule 1 boosts orders at the downstream node when backlog is high and pipeline is low relative to recent demand. Rule 2 boosts orders at the regional warehouse when its backlog is high and pipeline is low. Rule 3 reduces orders at any node when pipeline is excessive relative to recent demand, avoiding redundant orders. Rule 4 reduces orders when demand growth is low, preventing persistent over-ordering after demand subsides.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 10 and pipeline < recent * 4",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, (backlog - 10) / 2))"
    },
    {
      "when": "agent == 1 and backlog > 10 and pipeline < recent * 4",
      "delta": "min(6, max(0, (backlog - 10) / 2))"
    },
    {
